      "value": "I note that 2021.3.2p1 release notes say \"- Fixed issue where SerializedAssets would be removed from UdonBehaviours in the Editor\", but it does not seem that this is fixed in the current released SDK.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-14T22:45:19.993Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In some cases, a prefab containing an UdonBehaviour can end up with a null serializedProgramAsset, even though the referenced UdonProgramSource has a serialized program asset associated with it. This then results in a failure to load the program:\n\n```\n[<color=yellow>UdonBehaviour</color>] Could not load the program; the UdonBehaviour on 'SpherePrefab(Clone)' will not run.\nUnityEngine.Debug:Log (object,UnityEngine.Object)\nVRC.Core.Logger:Log (string,int,UnityEngine.Object)\nVRC.Udon.UdonBehaviour:InitializeUdonContent () (at Assets/Udon/UdonBehaviour.cs:1143)\nVRC.Udon.UdonManager:RegisterUdonBehaviour (VRC.Udon.UdonBehaviour) (at Assets/Udon/UdonManager.cs:668)\nVRC.Udon.Wrapper.Modules.ExternVRCInstantiate:__Instantiate__UnityEngineGameObject__UnityEngineGameObject (VRC.Udon.Common.Interfaces.IUdonHeap,uint[]) (at Assets/Udon/WrapperModules/ExternVRCInstantiate.cs:69)\nVRC.Udon.VM.UdonVM:Interpret ()\nVRC.Udon.UdonBehaviour:RunProgram (uint) (at Assets/Udon/UdonBehaviour.cs:884)\nVRC.Udon.UdonBehaviour:RunEvent (string,System.ValueTuple`2<string, object>[]) (at Assets/Udon/UdonBehaviour.cs:1066)\nVRC.Udon.UdonBehaviour:ManagedUpdate () (at Assets/Udon/UdonBehaviour.cs:447)\nVRC.Udon.UdonManager:Update () (at Assets/Udon/UdonManager.cs:251)\n```\n\nThis issue has cropped up a few times in the wild, and with the help of Haï~ I have a minimal repro procedure (using only Udon Graph, to make sure it's not an U# bug):\n\n1. Create a new project and import VRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.08.11.15.16_Public\n2. Import this unitypackage: https://www.dropbox.com/s/572efzuno9xvbbm/fails%20to%20set%20serialized%20program%20source.unitypackage?dl=0\n3. Initially, if you enter play mode, you will see two spheres, which both turn green. One is a spawned prefab, one is a prefab instance present from scene load.\n4. Delete the SerializedUdonPrograms folder.\n5. Enter play mode again. You'll see two spheres, but only one will turn green; the spawned prefab will fail to load its udon program with the stacktrace above.\n\nOnce in this state, editing or recompiling the udon program does not fix it; however, it can be fixed by opening and closing the prefab.\nI'm pretty sure there are other ways to enter this state than deleting the SerializedUdonPrograms directory, but this is the only consistent repro procedure we've found so far.",
